L32_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_DANMACHI_C_BELL_RA"
L33_1 = [[
Bell Cranel is the captain of the Hestia Familia, who is highly trusted by its members.
As a child, he was raised by his grandfather who told him heroic tales, inspiring Bell's desire to become one himself. Around a year after losing his only family, Bell ventured to The Labyrinth City Orario in pursuit of encounters and adventure.
Upon his arrival in Orario, his weak appearance caused most of the Familia to reject him. However, after meeting Hestia and becoming her first and only follower, Bell obtained a rare skill, Liaris Freese, that allows Bell to grow at an extraordinary pace through his admiration for Ais Wallenstein combined with his determination. Furthermore, due to his rapid progress and striking appearance, he has become famous and nicknamed Record Holder.
Due to his agility and rabbit-like appearance, he is also known as Rabbit's Foot. However, in battle, he displays calm leadership and strong mental fortitude, embodying the qualities of a seasoned Adventurer.
This resilience shines brightest in critical situations, and his unwavering resolve in the face of hardship is nothing short of heroic.]]
L31_1[1] = L32_1
L31_1[2] = L33_1
L32_1 = {}
L33_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_DANMACHI_CA_AIS"
L34_1 = [[
Ais Wallenstein is a first-class Adventurer and the pillar of the Loki Familia, the most prominent faction in The Labyrinth City Orario.
Known as Sword Princess, her legendary feats, such as single-handedly defeating the Floor Boss on the 37th floor, are too numerous to count. With beauty that rivals a goddess, she has earned widespread fame throughout Orario.
Ais harbors a deep hatred for monsters, and this strong emotion drives her to become ever more powerful.
She excels in close combat, using her skills and quick thinking alongside her magical abilities, including her signature wind element enchant magic, Ariel, to overwhelm her enemies.]]
L32_1[1] = L33_1
L32_1[2] = L34_1
L33_1 = {}
L34_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_DANMACHI_C_RYU_RA"
L35_1 = [[
Ryu Lion is a former Adventurer now working as an employee at The "Hostess of Fertility".
Once the sole survivor of her Familia, which was wiped out in a brutal massacre, Ryu found freedom from her painful past through her deep bond with Bell and his unyielding resolve. She possesses a strong sense of justice and will not hesitate to lend a hand when her companions are in danger.
Her cold, detached appearance and straightforward demeanor often lead others to misunderstand her, but in reality, she is kindhearted, pure, and a bit clumsy. Her views on romance, which are so innocent that even other Elves shake their heads, are a testament to her sincere nature.
As an Elf, a race naturally gifted in magic, Ryu excels in powerful spellcasting, healing abilities, and close combat, making her a highly versatile adventurer. Her extensive experience and remarkable skill make her an exceptional veteran, capable of handling even the most dangerous solo missions with confidence.]]
L33_1[1] = L34_1
L33_1[2] = L35_1
L34_1 = {}
L35_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_HESTIA"
L36_1 = [[
Hestia is one of the three great virgin goddesses and the goddess of the furnace who presides over flames.
Her role as a goddess of a Familia truly began when she crossed paths with Bell. Although she is known for being lazy and obsessively devoted to him, she is also a compassionate and caring goddess who treasures her children, earning strong trust and affection from her Familia. Hestia treats her Familia like her own family, and with her endearing appearance and playful personality, she is often regarded as the beloved mascot of her group.
Despite these endearing qualities, she still has a considerable debt to repay in order to provide Bell with his Hestia Knife, leading her to devote herself wholeheartedly to her part-time job at the Potato Poppers stand.]]
L34_1[1] = L35_1
L34_1[2] = L36_1
